  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the move with the rotary words (`fanuc.cps` `traverseZ`, `xyFirst`, `onRapid`). On a machine whose table tilts the work, the X/Y traverse of a 3+2 plane or of a cross drill runs at the pose that the previous program left. The #2987 law reads these operations only at their own pose.\n\n- `first_traverse_posed::posed_kind`: the posed law of #3084 now also reads each kind that carries a `Tilt` (the 3+2 planes) and the cross drill. Everything else in `turn_of` is unchanged: the sphere about the WCS origin for two work-turning rotaries, a full turn about the line for one, and the refusal by name of a rotary with no line.\n- `table_top` and `table_stays`: when every tilting rotary turns the work, the law reads the machine table fixed where it stands. The table does not turn. When a head tilts, the #2987 table law reads the table, as before.\n- The op stamp word of #3084 now also covers these operations. So their caches read Stale once.\n- `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj`: three operation stamps change. The stamp values come from the test's own path (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`). `first-4axis-part.nc` is byte-identical, and no operation is refused.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3100-table-tilt-first-traverse.md`.\n\n## Coordinator decisions (recorded in the decision file)\n\n1. The table is read fixed where it stands, not swept. A swept travel box refuses every 3+2 program.\n2. A test fixture change in `first_traverse_table.rs`. The test `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work` sets the WCS origin to zero for `Rig::Work`.\n   - Before: it expected no verdict.\n   - Now: it expects the verdict of the block corner on its sphere (29.584, from the stock, not the table) at 20 over the plane origin, and a pass at 30.\n3. The example restamp is stamp-only, and every `.nc` is byte-identical. The `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` save also rewrites fields that drifted on main before this PR (A `feed` / `travel`, `chain_order`, the machine `post`). It also writes a local absolute model path. So the PR takes only its three stamp values.\n4. The cross drill: the one shipped mill-turn (`assets/machines/millturn.mch`) states only a C along Z, with the head under it. So no shipped mill-turn changes, and there is no end-to-end pin for the cross drill.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse_table_tilt`:\n  - `a_3_2_plane_under_the_work_a_turning_table_can_leave_turned_up_is_refused_by_name` (A table, A 30, top 18.735)\n  - `a_3_2_plane_over_every_pose_of_a_turning_table_passes` (A table; trunnion B 30)\n- `first_traverse_table`: `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work` (changed, see above)\n- lib: `operation::first_traverse_posed::tests::the_fixed_table_reads_its_top_in_the_paths_height_scale`\n\n## Readings (debug, head a1a3e8391; the later commits change only docs)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app`, all green:\n- `--lib`\n- `first_traverse_table_tilt`, `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse_posed`, `first_traverse_rotary`\n- `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`\n- `first_4axis_part`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `machine`, `microarc_test_part`, `tilt_basis_compat`, `tormach_fourth_axis`\n- `first_traverse_mill_turn`, `first_traverse_rotary_mill_turn`\n- `drilling_cross`, `drilling_cross_rapids`, `drilling_cross_spindle`, `drilling_cross_part`, `drilling_cross_stock`, `drilling_cross_box`, `drilling_cross_holder`\n- `lathe_cross_drill`, `coarse_cross_drill`, `cross_drill_neighbours`, `stock_source_cross_drill`, `stitch_cross`\n- `example_catalog`\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nHeavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` reaches the app heavy lanes (every target). Not run, covered by the cut gate.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The cross drill end to end. No shipped mill-turn states a tilting rotary that turns the work.\n- `tormach.cps` turns A before the X/Y traverse. The law reads every pose there too (a superset, see the decision file).\n- The full quick gate. Only the binaries listed above were run.\n\nChangelog: The first traverse of a 3+2 plane and of a cross drill, on a machine whose table tilts the work, is now judged through every pose that the previous program can leave; a clearance under the work turned up is refused by name.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation).\n\nFixes #3100\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
